Changes from 1.1
----------------
- fixed problem with mulli instruction where the lower 8 bits
  of a result were always set to 0x15
- fixed problem with the calculation of the upper 32bits of
  64bit results from multiplications
- fixed problem where the overflow-bits(OV,SO) were not set
  correctly with most instructions(e.g. addco.,subfo.)
- the disassembler now supports most 64bit (PPC620) and FPU
  instructions

Description
-----------
This is a Emulator/Disassembler intended for Assembler programmers
wanting to develop PowerPC-routines on their 680x0 Amigas. To enable
output, special meaning has been given to the instruction "sc" which
makes calls to 680x0-AmigaOS possible(this is of course incompatible
with PPC-system-calls in PowerUp-Amigas).

